Massive update
I have rewritten  MZ to PIXIJS V8 It is still in development and being tested but Bitmap and Sprite perfectly work and behave.
I also have decoupled a lots of the limitations that was given in rpg maker MZ original code base (More flexible filter handlings, Built-in functions helpers to helps programmers
and Fully Typed TS rewrite and use modern convention. It behaves likes an ESM module and in the future you will be able to literally do plugins like module packages.
Many of the caveat is now that pixijs is mostly Async so a lots of the operations for rpg maker will shift towards a more Asynchronous approach
Some sample of how it will work :
Code:
class MyCustomClass extends SceneBase {

  // no need for constructor in heritance

  // Mainly for TS to stop complaining about non standards constructor
  override initialize(...args: any[]){
    // some initialization code
    super.initialize(...args);
  }

  override preload(){
    ImageManager.queue("texturefolder", "texturePath"); // user can queue a preload to be fired at start of the scene.
    ImageManager.queue("texturefolder", "texture", LoadingType.BACKGROUND); // here we tell the engine to not Lock the engine and just load it in the background!
  }

  foo(){
    // in this context we do not have an async way but we can tell the system to lock like standard rpg maker
    ImageManager.load("texturefolder", "texturePath");

  }

  async bar(){
    await ImageManager.loadAsync("texturefolder", "texturePath"); // in thise case we locking  the thread but in a async fashion. 
                                                                  // Async will automatically tell the Engine that the scene is not ready
  }


}
ALL of this code is still quite experimental and might change!
